// Module `args`: Args, the run's argument strings (PROG-3), an opaque own type granted
// to `main` and passed as a view. Both operations are CORE, restated. The strings are
// owned by the run, never charged to a task limit.

/// CORE. Number of arguments, the program name excluded. Cost: O(1). Ex: `args.len(a)`
pub fn len(a: Args) -> u64

/// CORE. A view of argument i (0 is the first after the program name), or None.
/// View: anchored to a; FREEZE a (it is never written anyway). Cost: O(1).
/// Ex: `let Some(input) = args.get(a, 0) else { return Error(Usage) }`
pub fn get(a: Args, i: u64) -> Option[View[String]] in a
